    <p>
      I'm Cole Saseen. I invest in public equities with a concentrated,
      activist-minded approach, and I write here about how I think — markets,
      capital allocation, and the case for owning few things with conviction.
    </p>
    <p>

    </p>
    <p>
      The method is top-down, then bottom-up: read the macro terrain, find the
      businesses that survive and compound through it, and size the handful
      where the crowd has the price wrong. I would rather hold cash than own
      something I cannot defend.
    </p>
    <p>

    </p>
